& [Phase8FPGAExecutionProfiles] is implement CEB-021 through CEB-030 only when separately activated
  + [depends_on] is stable software protocol, deterministic software oracle, measured workload, explicit device target, and hardware threat model
  + [track_1] is define bounded Cantor bytecode, prove a software interpreter model, then implement one FPGA interpreter
  + [track_2] is identify one measured hotspot, lower a static Cantor kernel through hardware IR or HLS to RTL, then synthesize one native profile
  + [shared_proof] is Rust, interpreter model, RTL simulation, synthesis, hardware-in-loop, and cross-profile normalized-result equivalence
  + [measure] is latency, throughput, area, memory, power estimate, compile time, and reconfiguration cost
  + [adoption] is optional and target-specific; neither track changes semantic authority
  + [rejection] is preserve software operation when hardware cost, mismatch, or trust risk outweighs measured gain

& [GlobalVerification] is required at every phase
  + [commands] is cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy with warnings denied, debug and overflow-checked release tests, locked offline tests, release build, documentation build, and dependency advisory audit
  + [trace] is every requirement maps to a fixture, proof, fault, or explicit gap
  + [change_control] is update source lineage, specification, feature support, narrative, and turn archive when understanding or authority changes
  + [stop_rule] is stop expanding when the active slice passes and the next slice is not yet dependency-ready
